<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anfal campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran-iraq-war">Iran–Iraq War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anfal campaign was a genocidal operation by the Iraqi government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurds">Kurds</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, at its height in 1988 during the last phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran-iraq-war">Iran–Iraq War</a>. Commanded by Ali Hassan al-Majid, it destroyed thousands of villages, used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-weapons">chemical weapons</a> and killed an estimated 50,000 to 100,000 people. Iraqi courts later convicted its leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> and crimes against humanity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anfal-campaign.jpg" alt="Anfal campaign" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob984 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iraqi_Kurdistan_in_Iraq_(disputed_hatched).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
